# U30 Air charge2 `@@MU300_CHARGE2_RELEASE_ID@@`

This release packages the reviewed charge2 source for the ZTE U30 Air with Linux `@@MU300_CHARGE2_KERNEL_RELEASE@@` and OpenWrt 25.12.5.

## Changes

- Adds the CPU and traffic LuCI/runtime integration, SMS and AT improvements, and saved user-package recovery to the charge2 image.
- Includes the reviewed Wi-Fi/WCN, DFS, IPv6 and updater-check source changes. Online kernel, boot and whole-system apply operations remain blocked; use the matching offline firmware package for upgrades.
- Adds the release-local `mu300-native-kmod-compat` provider. It records the kernel capabilities that are built in or supplied by the matching 7.2.9 kernel and does not ship kernel modules. Its device-side guard checks the exact kernel release, configuration, module hashes and built-in list before package changes.
- Creates the traffic service shutdown link so its final accounting hook runs before shutdown.

## Build and hardware status

The candidate kernel bundle is reused from the audited `charge2-test1-20261012` build. The release builder compares every recorded upstream kernel input and build log with this release's committed source and records the original build commit. The OpenWrt rootfs and local native-kmod package are assembled for this release ID and carry SHA-256 manifests.

The exact r2 package has not been installed or booted as a whole. Earlier test-candidate device checks do not substitute for validation of this full package. No claim is made that the r2 package has passed a complete hardware test.

## Install

Download the single complete `U30 Air Openwrt -r2.zip` firmware asset from the GitHub release and extract it; no split parts or reassembly script are needed. Run `install-u30air-host.ps1`, then use `-VerifyOnly` to check package assets without accessing the device. The package targets the rooted ZTE U30 Air and keeps Android as the default boot system.
